---
import Home from '../layouts/Home.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
---

<Home title="Privacy: Anthony" description="What this site collects (nothing), and what GitHub Pages logs.">
  <article class="container prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: 28 September 2026</p>

    <p>
      This page covers anthonyf2312.github.io, run by Anthony (<ExternalLink href="https://github.com/anthonyf2312"
        arrow={false}>@anthonyf2312</ExternalLink
      >), an individual in the United Kingdom. Patchr has <a href="/patchr/privacy/">its own privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. There are no forms, no accounts, no analytics, no tracking and no embedded content from other sites.
      Fonts and images are served from this site itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies. If you use the light and dark switch, your choice is kept in your own browser
      (local storage) so the site remembers it. It never leaves your device, and clearing your browser’s site data
      removes it.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub records visitors’ IP addresses for security, under
      <ExternalLink href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        >GitHub’s privacy statement</ExternalLink
      >. Anthony doesn’t see or receive that data.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>Links to other sites open in a new tab. Their own privacy policies apply once you’re there.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under UK data protection law you can ask what data is held about you, and complain to the
      <ExternalLink href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner’s Office</ExternalLink> if you’re
      unhappy. For anything about this page, open an issue or message
      <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/anthonyf2312" arrow={false}>@anthonyf2312</ExternalLink> on GitHub.
    </p>
  </article>
</Home>
